<td id="S2.T2.2.7.7" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:1.3pt;padding-right:1.3pt;">76.5</td>
<td id="S2.T2.2.7.8" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_r" style="padding-left:1.3pt;padding-right:1.3pt;">79.8</td>
<td id="S2.T2.2.7.9" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:1.3pt;padding-right:1.3pt;">46.0</td>
<td id="S2.T2.2.7.10" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:1.3pt;padding-right:1.3pt;">23.9</td>
<td id="S2.T2.2.7.11" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:1.3pt;padding-right:1.3pt;">43.8</td></tr>
<tr id="S2.T2.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S2.T2.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:1.3pt;padding-right:1.3pt;">1.0</th>
<th id="S2.T2.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r" style="padding-left:1.3pt;padding-right:1.3pt;">0.86</th>
<td id="S2.T2.2.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:1.3pt;padding-right:1.3pt;">73.3</td>
<td id="S2.T2.2.8.4" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:1.3pt;padding-right:1.3pt;">54.3</td>
<td id="S2.T2.2.8.5" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r" style="padding-left:1.3pt;padding-right:1.3pt;">63.2</td>
<td id="S2.T2.2.8.6" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:1.3pt;padding-right:1.3pt;">88.5</td>
<td id="S2.T2.2.8.7" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:1.3pt;padding-right:1.3pt;">74.3</td>
<td id="S2.T2.2.8.8" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r" style="padding-left:1.3pt;padding-right:1.3pt;">78.5</td>
<td id="S2.T2.2.8.9" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:1.3pt;padding-right:1.3pt;"><span id="S2.T2.2.8.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">47.7</span></td>
<td id="S2.T2.2.8.10" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:1.3pt;padding-right:1.3pt;">23.5</td>
<td id="S2.T2.2.8.11" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:1.3pt;padding-right:1.3pt;"><span id="S2.T2.2.8.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">44.2</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Post-intervention scores with different <math id="S2.T2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> values. <math id="S2.T2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, R0.5, and R0.7 represent mIoU, recall at IoU thresholds of 0.5 and 0.7.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The post-intervention discriminability scores and consistency scores are presented in Table <a href="#S2.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 2.3 Causal Intervention ‣ 2 Exploring Temporal Logic Consistency ‣ Improving Temporal Understanding Logic Consistency in Video-Language Models via Attention Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
As shown in the table, mild interventions effectively improve the model’s performance and consistency across the three subsets, while overly strong interventions lead to performance degradation. Additionally, relatively mild interventions are sufficient to enhance the model’s <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{rg.}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{rg.}</annotation></semantics></math>, whereas improving <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{sg.}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{sg.}</annotation></semantics></math> requires stronger intervention intensity, indicating that the shifted grounding task poses greater challenges for the model in maintaining consistent outputs. These results demonstrate a clear causal relationship between attention discriminability and temporal logic consistency.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.4 </span>Generalizability Analysis</h3>

<div id="S2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To validate the generalizability of our conclusions across other models and tasks, we extend the analysis to the Qwen2.5-VL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai et al. (2025)</a></cite>. Furthermore, we select the Event Order Judgment (EOJ) task as a representative one of complex temporal reasoning tasks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yu et al. (2023)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Swetha et al. (2025)</a></cite>, which involves temporal order judgment, allowing us to further investigate the model’s temporal capabilities in complex multi-event scenarios.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.08138v1/qwen_eoj_violin.png" id="S2.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/201;" width="429" height="201" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>Violin plot of analysis results on EOJ task.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S2.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In the EOJ task, we define a new consistency score and an attention discriminability score to verify our findings. The distribution of attention discriminability scores for different ranges of consistency scores is shown as a violin plot in Figure <a href="#S2.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ 2.4 Generalizability Analysis ‣ 2 Exploring Temporal Logic Consistency ‣ Improving Temporal Understanding Logic Consistency in Video-Language Models via Attention Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. We observe a significant positive correlation (Pearson correlation coefficient is <math id="S2.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.447" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.447</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.447</annotation></semantics></math>), consistent with the trend found in TimeChat. This demonstrates that the relationship between attention discriminability and temporal logic consistency holds true for other leading Video-LLMs. The detailed implementation can be found in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS3" title="A.3 Details of Analysis on EOJ Task ‣ Appendix A More Details about Analysis ‣ Improving Temporal Understanding Logic Consistency in Video-Language Models via Attention Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Attention Enhancement</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the previous section, it is confirmed that the temporal discriminability of cross-modal attention heads is a key factor influencing the model’s temporal logic consistency. <span id="S3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">How can we enhance attention discriminability to improve temporal consistency?</span> To achieve generalization and cross-architecture applicability, we formulate the attention discriminability enhancement as an optimization objective termed <span id="S3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">T</span>emporally <span id="S3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">C</span>onditioned <span id="S3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">A</span>ttention <span id="S3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">S</span>harpening Loss (<span id="S3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TCAS</span> Loss). The specific loss computation is detailed in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3 Attention Enhancement ‣ Improving Temporal Understanding Logic Consistency in Video-Language Models via Attention Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, where the <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{SelectTopHeads}(H,S,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">SelectTopHeads</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{SelectTopHeads}(H,S,t)</annotation></semantics></math> means selecting the top <math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> attention heads from the set of all heads <math id="S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> based on scores <math id="S3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> TCAS Loss</figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="alg1.4" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom"><span id="alg1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input</span>: Video and text tokens <math id="alg1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V,T</annotation></semantics></math>, model <math id="alg1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="alg1.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parameter</span>: Top heads number <math id="alg1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, margin <math id="alg1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, threshold <math id="alg1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="thr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">thr</annotation></semantics></math> 
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="alg1.4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output</span>: TCAS loss <math id="alg1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math></p></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="alg1.5" class="ltx_listing ltx_figure_panel ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
           Response <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, attentions <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{H}\leftarrow M(V,T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>H</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{H}\leftarrow M(V,T)</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
           Compute <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{v}_{cross.}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{v}_{cross.}</annotation></semantics></math> using Equation (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2.1 Detection and Interpretation ‣ 2 Exploring Temporal Logic Consistency ‣ Improving Temporal Understanding Logic Consistency in Video-Language Models via Attention Enhancement" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
           <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{t}\leftarrow\textsc{SelectTopHeads}(H,S^{v}_{cross.},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">SelectTopHeads</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>H</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{t}\leftarrow\textsc{SelectTopHeads}(H,S^{v}_{cross.},t)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each head <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
            Aggregate visual tokens in <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{h}_{T,V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{h}_{T,V}</annotation></semantics></math> according to timestamps to get <math id="alg1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{h}_{T,V_{time}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{h}_{T,V_{time}}</annotation></semantics></math> 
</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{h}_{valid}\leftarrow\{q\in T\mid\text{Max}(A^{h}_{q,V_{time}})&gt;thr\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Max</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{h}_{valid}\leftarrow\{q\in T\mid\text{Max}(A^{h}_{q,V_{time}})&gt;thr\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each text query token <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{h}_{valid}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{h}_{valid}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
             Mean <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{h}_{q}=\sum_{k\in V_{time}}(A^{h}_{q,k})/|V_{time}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{h}_{q}=\sum_{k\in V_{time}}(A^{h}_{q,k})/|V_{time}|</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
             Pos. <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{h}_{q}\leftarrow\{A^{h}_{q,k}\in A^{h}_{q,V_{time}}\mid A^{h}_{q,k}&gt;M^{h}_{q}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>&gt;</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{h}_{q}\leftarrow\{A^{h}_{q,k}\in A^{h}_{q,V_{time}}\mid A^{h}_{q,k}&gt;M^{h}_{q}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
             Neg. <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N^{h}_{q}\leftarrow\{A^{h}_{q,k}\in A^{h}_{q,V_{time}}\mid A^{h}_{q,k}&lt;M^{h}_{q}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>&lt;</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N^{h}_{q}\leftarrow\{A^{h}_{q,k}\in A^{h}_{q,V_{time}}\mid A^{h}_{q,k}&lt;M^{h}_{q}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
            
             Loss <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{h}_{q}=\text{Max}(m+\text{Max}(N^{h}_{q})-\text{Min}(P^{h}_{q}),0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Max</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>Max</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>Min</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{h}_{q}=\text{Max}(m+\text{Max}(N^{h}_{q})-\text{Min}(P^{h}_{q}),0)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  <math id="alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\sum\limits_{h\in H_{t}}\sum_{q\in T^{h}_{valid}}\mathcal{L}^{h}_{q})/(\sum\limits_{h\in H_{t}}|T^{h}_{valid}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\sum\limits_{h\in H_{t}}\sum_{q\in T^{h}_{valid}}\mathcal{L}^{h}_{q})/(\sum\limits_{h\in H_{t}}|T^{h}_{valid}|)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We first identify the attention heads with the highest cross-modal scores and the text tokens that focus on specific video timestamps. This approach preserves the original contextual interaction capabilities of the attention heads. A contrastive learning loss is designed for the selected text query tokens to amplify the differences in attention scores across distinct timestamps, thereby compelling the attention heads to make explicit relevance judgments for temporally distributed information. We use weight <math id="S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{ae}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{ae}</annotation></semantics></math> to balance the TCAS loss and next token prediction loss. Our method introduces no additional modules, ensuring compatibility with various transformer-based architectures <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vaswani et al. (2023)</a></cite>. Furthermore, it does not depend on specific text templates or video patterns, making it broadly applicable to diverse video-language tasks.</p>
</div>
